Carried patch, Windows only: Palace's C++ under MinGW.

Three causes, five files: M_PI needs _USE_MATH_DEFINES under -std=c++17
(one target_compile_definitions under if(MINGW)); std::filesystem::path does
not convert to std::string where its value_type is wchar_t (a
TableWithCSVFile constructor taking a path, and .string() at five sites);
std::max(0L, memory) where std::distance returns long long on LLP64. All
portable: identical behaviour on Linux and macOS.

diff --git a/palace/CMakeLists.txt b/palace/CMakeLists.txt
index 4816f3a..3370210 100644
--- a/palace/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/palace/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -299,6 +299,10 @@ endif()
 set(LIB_TARGET_NAME libpalace)
 add_library(${LIB_TARGET_NAME} "")
 target_include_directories(${LIB_TARGET_NAME} PUBLIC ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR})
+# MinGW's <math.h> defines M_PI only with _USE_MATH_DEFINES under strict -std=c++17.
+if(MINGW)
+  target_compile_definitions(${LIB_TARGET_NAME} PUBLIC _USE_MATH_DEFINES)
+endif()
 target_include_directories(${LIB_TARGET_NAME} PUBLIC ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/generated)
 
